[h1]Print Extension List[/h1]

[h2][b]Features[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] Mod developers can include this as a dependency, allowing users to easily export their mod list to the debug log.
[*] On UI startup, writes a report to the debug log containing:
[list]
[*] Game version.
[*] Current screen resolution and the UI settings that affect menu layout: UI scale and menu width options, the engine UI scale values, and the Helper view size, [b]uiScale[/b] and [b]scaleX[/b]/[b]scaleY[/b] results.
[*] Every enabled DLC (id, name, version, date, location and other fields).
[*] Every enabled extension/mod (id, name, author, source, version, date, location and other fields).
[/list]
[*] Flags likely broken mod installs right in the Options menu, using only texts the game already ships in every language:
[list]
[*] An extension whose folder is named like a Steam Workshop item ([b]ws_<number>[/b]) while the game does not manage it as a subscription - typically a hand-copied or unsubscribed leftover that will never update.
[*] The same extension id installed into two different folders.
[*] A flagged extension gets the standard warning icon on [b]Settings[/b] and on [b]Extensions[/b], a warning-coloured row in the extension list, and the details in the info panel beside it.
[/list]
[/list]
[h2][b]Limitations[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] The report itself is debug-log only; the only in-game output is the warning marking in the Options menu.
[*] No configuration - it always logs once per UI load.
[/list]
[h2][b]Requirements[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]X4: Foundations[/b] 8.00 or newer.
[/list]
[h2][b]Installation[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Steam Workshop[/b] - [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3770927339]Print Extension List[/url]
[*] [b]Nexus Mods[/b] - [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/x4foundations/mods/2191]Print Extension List[/url]
[/list]
[h2][b]Save state[/b][/h2]

[b]No[/b] (removing the extension does not break saves).

[h2][b]Usage[/b][/h2]

Install and enable the extension. On the next game start look in the debug log for [b][General][/b] lines containing the prefix [b]PrintExtensionList:[/b].

